---
id: org.dxos.review.assistant
name: Assistant
version: 0.1.0
---

Conventions for what goes into an agent's conversation that a linter cannot express. Each `rule`
block below is discovered by the agentic-review harness.

## Extensions

| Term   | URI                   |
| ------ | --------------------- |
| `rule` | org.dxos.mdl.rule@1.0 |

## Rules

```mdl
rule machine-written-prompt-text-is-synthetic: Text the reader did not write goes into a conversation as synthetic
  A user-role message is drawn as the reader's own words, so text that code places there on
  anyone else's behalf must carry `disposition: 'synthetic'`, which the chat draws as context
  instead of a user bubble. Flag a text block built for `submitPrompt`, `enqueueMessage`,
  `Agent.delegate`'s `message`, `RunPromptInChat`, or a feed append with a user sender when its
  text comes from another session or agent (delegation, a relay), a trigger, a resumed question,
  a recovered tool result, or a runtime note such as "You have been assigned the task below.",
  and the block has no `disposition: 'synthetic'`. Flag code that forwards caller-supplied blocks
  into another conversation unchanged when the caller is not the reader. Do not flag text the
  reader typed or chose (the prompt input, a suggestion chip they clicked), a test fixture that
  stands in for the reader, or a block whose disposition is set by a helper that already marks
  it. Fix: set `disposition: 'synthetic'` where the block is built, or map forwarded text blocks
  to it at the hand-over (see `delegateToSession` in
  `packages/core/compute/agent-runtime/src/agent-service/AgentService.ts`).
  scope: repo
  files:
    - packages/**/src/**/*.ts
    - packages/**/src/**/*.tsx
  grep: submitPrompt|enqueueMessage|delegate\(|RunPromptInChat|_tag: 'text'|Text\.make\(
  unit: file
  context: diff
  system-one: on
  severity: warn
  question: Does this change put text the reader did not write into a conversation as a user-role text block without `disposition: 'synthetic'`?
```

## Appendix

```mdl
ext rule
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.rule@1.0
  desc: A machine-checked review rule applied by an LLM subagent or the System One checker.
  inline-prose: true
  fields:
    files:       Glob | Glob[]     # paths this rule reviews, relative to `scope`
    grep?:       Prose             # optional regex pre-filter over file contents
    severity?:   warn | error      # defaults to warn
    scope?:      dir | repo        # glob base: this file's dir (default) or repo root
    unit?:       file | pr         # one verdict per file (default) or per change set
    context?:    ContextKind[]     # diff | imports | importers | siblings | package | public-api | similar | test | pr
    system-one?: on | off          # off when no fetcher can supply what the rule needs
    question?:   Prose             # literal yes/no question for the System One checker
```
